---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/urls';
import '../../styles/global.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Kindness Score — KindNesta"
  description="How KindNesta’s EU-aligned Kindness Score works — for retail and enterprise buyers comparing products on our B2B marketplace."
>
  <section class="page-hero reveal">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section__eyebrow">Transparency</span>
      <h1>Kindness Score</h1>
      <p>
        A 0–100 rating that helps B2B buyers compare products across the KindNesta catalogue with
        clearer evidence — informed by European green-claim, packaging, chemical, and
        product-passport expectations. Scores are KindNesta’s internal rating and stay
        <strong>provisional</strong> until evidence is verified.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href={withBase('products/')}>Browse catalogue</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={withBase('contact/?interest=quote')} style="margin-left: 0.5rem;">Request a quote</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section reveal" style="padding-top: 1rem;">
    <div class="container prose-page">
      <div class="score-bands" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <span data-band="high">80–100 Strong</span>
        <span data-band="mid">50–79 Good</span>
        <span data-band="low">0–49 Fair</span>
      </div>

      <h2>What the score is (and is not)</h2>
      <p>
        The Kindness Score is KindNesta’s internal comparison tool. It is <strong>not</strong> a
        third-party life-cycle assessment, PEF study, or official EU ecolabel. We show it so buyers
        can see how much verifiable evidence sits behind a product story.
      </p>

      <h2>Why Europe shapes the rules</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>EmpCo (Directive 2024/825)</strong> — from 27 Sep 2026, generic “eco/green/sustainable”
          claims and many self-made sustainability labels face strict limits.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>PPWR (EU 2025/40)</strong> — packaging recyclability, recycled content, and waste
          prevention expectations.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>REACH</strong> — chemical safety and substances of very high concern.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>ESPR / Digital Product Passport</strong> — growing demand for composition,
          origin, and circularity data (textiles are a priority).
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How scoring works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Gate checks (A1–A7)</strong> — claim hygiene, REACH baseline, evidence age,
          trade-off honesty. Any Fail caps the score at 49 and blocks weak claims.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Evidence pillars (B1–B6)</strong> — chemicals, material %, certifications,
          circularity, shipped packaging, traceability.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>KindNesta review</strong> — we confirm documents before treating a score as
          verified.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Do products need certificates to appear here?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>To be listed:</strong> basic product data and honest descriptions. Chemical
        compliance expectations still apply for EU-bound goods.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>To make green claims or earn Strong scores:</strong> yes — claim-specific
        third-party proof. Typical schemes:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>GRS / RCS</strong> — recycled content chain of custody</li>
        <li><strong>GOTS</strong> — organic textiles</li>
        <li><strong>FSC / PEFC</strong> — responsible paper / forest fibre</li>
        <li><strong>OEKO-TEX Standard 100</strong> — harmful substance testing for textiles</li>
        <li><strong>EU Ecolabel / Blue Angel</strong> — broader “excellent performance” labels</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What buyers should check on a product page</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Score band + notes (why the number is what it is)</li>
        <li>Specific bullets (materials, certifications named)</li>
        <li>Product details table (materials, dimensions, browse node)</li>
        <li>Variant options under the same parent product</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Provisional scores</h2>
      <p>
        Some catalogue scores began from supplier listing text before full evidence packs
        arrived. Treat those as <strong>provisional</strong> until certificates, BOM %, and REACH
        statements are verified against our checklist.
      </p>

      <p style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href={withBase('docs/KINDNESS-SCORE-STANDARD.md')}>Download scoring standard</a>
        <a class="btn btn--secondary" href={withBase('partners/')} style="margin-left: 0.5rem;">Partner &amp; supplier hub</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
